# Dart source checks out with LF on every platform.
#
# Nineteen tests in test/ assert on the TEXT of a source file — they read it
# with readAsStringSync() and match a snippet. That makes the checkout's line
# endings part of the contract, and with core.autocrlf on (the default for the
# Windows tooling here) a fresh clone hands those tests CRLF while git stores
# LF. Two of them assert across a newline, so they passed on the macOS CI
# runner and failed the moment the repository was cloned on Windows — found
# exactly that way, cloning this app out on its own.
#
# The tests themselves now normalise before matching, which is the real fix;
# this keeps every checkout identical so the next multi-line assertion cannot
# reintroduce the same trap.
*.dart text eol=lf

# Gradle and shell tooling are read by Linux/macOS toolchains too.
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.kts    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
gradlew  text eol=lf

# Binary assets git must not touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.jks  binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk  binary
*.aab  binary
